   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Paper Tear\n\nThe outgoing scene is printed on paper that strains, rips down the middle with a jolt of the camera and a flash, and is flung apart in two torn halves with flying scraps, revealing the next scene. Built-in placeholder scenes A and B (the two .ptr-panel elements) make it preview on its own; to use it between your own scenes, replace the contents of those two panels with your scenes (or set them to your full-frame clips) and keep the block on a track above.\n\nCategory: transitions. Length: 1.2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A violent, physical scene change: a reveal, a breakthrough, a big announcement.\n- Scenes that already feel printed or poster-like.\n\nAvoid when:\n- Calm or elegant pieces where an impact would feel out of place.\n- Scenes with important content on the seam in the middle.\n\nVariables:\n- impact (number, 0-2): Impact, default 1\n- roughness (number, 0-1): Roughness, default 0.5\n- seed (number, 0-9999): Seed, default 7\n- edge_color (color): Edge color, default \"#FFFFFF\"\n- shadow_color (string): Shadow color, default \"rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45)\"\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
